    "field": "Integrated assessment of climate change",
    "problem": "Effectively informing political agreements on long-term climate goals is challenging because scientific analysis alone cannot determine a single best objective, requiring an integrated mapping of the consequences of different policy choices to account for diverse risks, uncertainties, and societal values.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a systematic mapping approach, based on scenario analysis, that explores the consequences of policy choices by linking long-term climate risks with the required temperature limits and emission reduction pathways to better inform decision-makers.",
    "task": "The task is to summarize and assess a mapping approach that systematically links climate change risks, temperature targets, and emission pathways to help decision-makers understand the consequences of different policy choices and better inform the public.",
